question 1] The terminal allows you to talk directly to your computer using text commands instead of clicking around.
• On Windows: Press the Windows Key, type PowerShell or Terminal, and hit Enter.
• On Mac: Press Cmd + Space to open Spotlight, type Terminal, and hit Enter.

question 2] We use the mkdir (make directory) command to generate new folders instantly.
1. In your open terminal, type the following command and hit Enter:bash
mkdir web-development-practice

2. Move your terminal's focus inside this new folder using the cd (change directory) command:bash
cd web-development-practice

question 3] Instead of creating them one by one, you can tell the terminal to make multiple folders all at once by separating their names with spaces.
1. Run this command in your terminal:bash
mkdir week-1 week-2 week-3

question 4] To create empty files from the terminal, we use different commands depending on your operating system. We will target the paths directly.
• If you are on a Mac or Linux terminal:bash
touch week-1/index.html week-2/index.html week-3/index.html

question 5] To satisfy the practice part of your assignment, run these quick trial commands to show your instructor you know how to manipulate files:
1. Navigate into a folder: cd week-1 (moves you in). Then type cd .. to go back up to the main folder.
2. Rename a folder: Let's pretend to rename week-3 to sandbox.
	• Mac/Linux: mv week-3 sandbox
	• Windows: Rename-Item week-3 sandbox
3. Delete a folder: Let's delete that newly renamed sandbox folder. Because it has files inside it, we use a recursive flag to force it to delete completely.
	• Mac/Linux: rm -rf sandbox
	• Windows: Remove-Item -Recurse sandbox

question 6] If you installed VS Code correctly with the "Add to PATH" option earlier, you can launch it instantly from the command line.
1. Make sure your terminal is still inside the main web-development-practice directory.
2. Type the shortcut command code followed by a . (the dot tells it to open the current folder):bash
code .


